        "id": 1115183
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-30T22:01:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The simpler approach makes sense. I think single per-task arrays still require something like a \"next_offset\" variable though. The offsets into per-task arrays can be stored in the per-cpu structs you described, but there needs to be a way of assigning those offsets in the first place.",
